From 02f7849c5401a7e2b1d964acba9b21e03392e4b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(front): warn of the subscript of [][Next]_v as TLC's
 SubscriptCollector does

TLC reads the subscript of the specification's [][Next]_v as it
processes the configuration (processConfigSpec): it collects the state
variables through tuples, LETs, labels, the operators it applies and
the definitions it holds as operators, ignores any other builtin and a
definition it holds as a value, and gives up at a number or a string.
It then warns that it can't tell (2139), or of each variable the
subscript lacks in its order of the variables (2140), between the
warnings about the invariants and those about the properties. The
front end printed neither: 24 runs of the upstream conformance suite
now print what TLC prints.

An operator's literal argument now keeps its expression
(Binding::Literal), which TLC's collector reads through the LazyValue
of a parameterized INSTANCE (Github687spec). A subscript the front end
can't follow, as one the configuration substitutes, leaves the
warnings unknown, which declines unless -nowarning drops them.
